WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:01:00.400
[music]

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:07.510
[Lepage] Everybody has these explanations for how&nbsp;
the theater started and as many tales many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:12.370
myths, but the one that I think suits me&nbsp;
the best is the idea that gazillions of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:17.710
years ago people gathered in a quarry and they&nbsp;
did a big bonfire and would tell stories&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:21.850
to each other and eventually somebody&nbsp;
had the idea of standing up and using&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.850 --> 00:01:26.140
his shadow to tell the story and that's&nbsp;
how theater is born. That's how film is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:30.550
born. That's how all the technologies we use&nbsp;
today to tell stories are born; they're born&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:36.340
from that moment of man realizing that he&nbsp;
can create figures that are larger than life.

00:01:37.031 --> 00:03:20.367
[music]

